<template id="rulesContent"><div class="rules-content"><ul><li>40 life each. Combat damage = max(0, attack − opponent block). Guarded Strike deals 2 direct damage after combat if it took no combat damage; direct damage bypasses block. Both retaliations resolve simultaneously without recursion. Total damage determines objectives, other damage triggers, and defeat before recovery.</li><li>Choose one main card and up to one other bonus burn from your active hand. Commit face down, then reveal together.</li><li>Normal cards return after damage. Burned cards are permanently discarded. A main cannot be a bonus or reaction burn, but a Purple-spending Charged Fist permanently burns the opposing main on hit after damage.</li><li>Players alternate one reaction burn or pass. Two consecutive passes close the window. First reaction priority alternates each round.</li><li>Reaction burns reveal immediately. Main abilities, bonuses, and reactions stack. Printed conditions use unmodified stats. On-hit and no-damage effects check final simultaneous damage.</li><li>Choose a listed bottom color, modified by card effects. Restrictions always leave a destination. If every destination is exhausted, choose any available hand. Driving Tackle can spend Orange to ignore 2 block and, on hit, choose one opposing legal next color to prohibit if more than one remains. After all route cuts, a Yellow-spending Driving Kick that hit chooses the opponent’s legal next hand. Resolve all forced destinations before normal hand selections; both normal next hands reveal together.</li><li>Eighteen main cards have objectives that earn advantage after final damage. Tokens persist across hands, capped at one per color. Select tokens through a spending main before committing; burns cannot spend them. Spent tokens are consumed on reveal even if their on-hit payoff fails. Combination Strike may spend any one color for +1 attack, or any two different colors instead for +4 attack, +2 block, and ignore 2 opposing block. Its token colors do not add destinations.</li><li>Rooted Guard sets up an independent objective: deal 4+ damage in the following round to earn Green advantage. It expires after that round; Counterpunch can deny the award. Outside Step gains +1 attack next round on hit, independently of its printed-block read. Rushdown and Glancing Step pressure adds 2 attack for the next round only. Glancing Step grants pressure and Yellow advantage after taking exactly 1 final damage; it does not require dealing damage. Driving Palm recovers at most 1 life per hit, capped at 40, and cannot prevent a knockout. Counterpunch can prevent this round’s advantage awards, including simultaneous objectives.</li><li>Darting Strike is 6/0. Declare its optional Yellow spend with the face-down commitment; the token is consumed on reveal even if you keep Darting Strike. Before reactions, keep it or permanently burn it to choose another available Yellow main. The committed bonus and carried effects stay. Replacement abilities and destinations apply, and printed-stat reads are recomputed. The replacement cannot spend advantage. If both players cancel, choices stay hidden until both decide. A Clinch Throw burn lock prevents cancelling.</li><li>Brace can spend Green to suppress the opponent’s carried attack bonus this round and prevent either fighter gaining attack bonuses for next round. It does not cancel delayed objectives. Mirror Step checks printed attack and block exactly 3 independently; spending Blue removes one held opposing token for dealing damage and another for taking no damage. Choose removals after damage and before new objective awards. Spent tokens cannot be removed. Clinch Throw can spend Orange to prevent opposing bonus and reaction burns in the following round on hit; mains, advantage spending, and involuntary main-card burns remain legal. Haymaker is 7/0; dealing no combat damage gives its owner -2 final block in the following round, to a minimum of 0. Carried effects are public and last for their stated round.</li><li>Zero life or no remaining cards loses the fight; simultaneous losses are a draw. Bot choices vary with the seed; combat itself has no randomness.</li></ul><p>All 36 cards are a provisional draft. No balance claims yet.</p></div></template>
